P-I5b, spec 001 W2: the edge's index function on the folders alone, and a folder's path to its slash, for the
Author's hand.

Built from plain copies: infra/prod/edge.tf as W1's thirteen patches leave it (a git archive export of 0bf73883, W1's
tip, with P-I3, P-G1, P-G3, P-I7, P-G4, P-G2, P-I4, P-G5, P-6, P-I5, P-G6, P-I6, and P-G7 applied in that order);
edited in $TMPDIR, then diff -u with a/ and b/ labels after this preamble; never git apply, and nothing written into
any worktree. A patch of its own, after P-I5, not a rebuilt P-I5: W1's gate commits P-I5 before W2's branch can, so
W2's change to edge.tf is a second patch on top of it. Apply it on W2's -p branch after P-W2, with
`patch -p1 < <this file>` at the repository's root, and commit the result byte for byte (tasks.md T175, T177).

What it holds (group 8's review B, the smaller ones, which W1's note put on W2's branch; plan.md §16, "W2, as
built"; contracts/edge.md §3):
  - h4-site-index on the folders' behaviors alone: `*/`, and each folder of the site's without its slash, /credits,
    /disclosure, and /status, after /api/*; the default behavior runs no function, so its cost is one invocation a
    folder page, not one a site request (research.md R-05);
  - the function redirects a folder's path without its slash to it, 301, as the web image's nginx does, where S3
    through origin access control answered AccessDenied.

Its checks, on a fresh export of W2's tip with W1's thirteen patches, P-W2, and this one, in that order: infra/test's
T104 checks pass (test_prod_cdn.py), with both switches off and on; on the same export without this patch,
check_index and check_distribution's ordered behaviors fail.
